### Important notes about the job and web session

- When you submit a job using this interface, a web session is created for you to interact with the job. 

- Closing your browser window or tab will NOT stop the running job or web session. Likewise, if you experience network issues, you may be disconnected from your web session and be returned to a login page, however the job and web session *will still be running*. You can reconnect freely using the Connect button below.  

- *Closing the application* within the web session *will* also stop the web session and then the job will be canceled; your browser will display a "Failed to connect" message.

- If you wish to stop the job and web session, please use the "Cancel" button above.

### Important notes about your Jupyter session

- When you submit a job, a Jupyter Notebook server is started for you in a secure container. Your selected Git repository will be cloned (or updated) in your home directory at `$HOME/my-useful-repo`.

- Closing your browser window or tab will **not** stop the running job or Jupyter server. If you disconnect, you can reconnect using the Connect button.

- Stopping the Jupyter server from within the web interface will end your session and cancel the job.

- To stop the job and session, use the "Cancel" button above in the Open OnDemand dashboard.
